# Editing down and up through the Today list with the arrow keys keeps the caret column, each change lands in its own project, and a creation key in Today adds nothing while x after it still marks the entry done.
file <<END
INBOX:
	- Call the plumber
	- Renew passport @due({today-3})
Work:
	- Write quarterly report @due({today-2})
	- Review pull requests
Home:
	- Pay rent @due({today-7})
END
keys gt <Enter> <Down>
type !
keys <Down>
type ?
keys <Up> <Up>
type #
keys <Esc>
see ▌ - Renew pas#sport  INBOX
see   - Write quarterl!y report  Work
see   - Pay rent?  Home
keys o x
see ▌ ✔ Renew pas#sport  INBOX
quit
saved <<END
INBOX:
	- Call the plumber
	- Renew pas#sport @due({today-3}) @done({today})
Work:
	- Write quarterl!y report @due({today-2})
	- Review pull requests
Home:
	- Pay rent? @due({today-7})
END
